Package: python3-paramiko-insecure
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
Recommends: python3-invoke,
Description: SSH2 for Python with BROKEN obsolete algorithms (paramiko_insecure)
 Treat a connection made with this module as no more private or trustworthy
 than telnet. Use it only on a physically secure or otherwise isolated
 network, and never across the public internet.
 .
 It is paramiko 5 with the obsolete SSH support that upstream removed in 4.0
 and 5.0 deliberately put back:
 .
  * DSA ("ssh-dss") host and user keys;
  * SHA-1 RSA signatures ("ssh-rsa");
  * SHA-1 key exchange: diffie-hellman-group1-sha1, diffie-hellman-group14-sha1
    and diffie-hellman-group-exchange-sha1, with 1024-bit group-exchange
    moduli.
 .
 Each of these is broken or so weakened that a capable attacker on the network
 path can be expected to read or alter the session. They were removed from
 OpenSSH and paramiko for good reason.
 .
 This package exists for one reason: hardware that is 20 years old or more,
 installed where replacing it is impossible, whose SSH server speaks nothing
 else. Where a device supports anything better, use python3-paramiko instead.
 .
 Scope is deliberately small: SSH sessions, SFTP and SCP. GSSAPI/Kerberos is
 removed entirely rather than restored.
 .
 The module is installed as "paramiko_insecure", so this package can be
 installed alongside python3-paramiko without affecting it. Code must opt in
 by name, with "import paramiko_insecure" -- never aliased to "paramiko".
